{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MTdid8YfS52Bj1RerRzdF5","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Writing Plan — CoRL 2026\\\\n# Paper: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\\\\n# Deadline: 2026-05-29 (14 days from today)\\\\n# Format: 8 pages + references\\\\n# Last updated: 2026-05-15 (D035: C6 seed count correction)\\\\n\\\\nvenue:\\\\n  name: CoRL 2026\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-29\\\\n  format: \\\\\\\"8 pages + unlimited references\\\\\\\"\\\\n  template: corl2026  # IEEE two-column\\\\n  positioning: diagnostic-analysis  # NOT method paper\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# PAPER STRUCTURE\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nsections:\\\\n  - id: abstract\\\\n    title: Abstract\\\\n    target_words: 200\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      Temporal abstraction via variable-dt imagination in world-model RL (DreamerV3) consistently degrades performance.\\\\n      We conduct a factorial diagnostic isolating trained dt_embedding as the reliable trigger for pathological value\\\\n      overestimation (nve>1.5x, 4/4 separating power across seeds). Collapse is stochastic (seed-dependent), but the\\\\n      diagnostic marker is deterministic. Practical mitigation: restrict imagination to dt=1 during multi-dt training\\\\n      → 95% baseline recovery (869.9@105K vs baseline 915.67). [D035: s2 RUNNING, update with multi-seed stats when done]\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C3, C6]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 8  # last\\\\n\\\\n  - id: introduction\\\\n    title: Introduction\\\\n    target_pages: 1.0\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal; world-model RL offers natural testbed via imagination dt.\\\\n      (2) Puzzle: all variable-rate attempts degrade. TAWM shows Δt conditioning works in MPC — why does it fail\\\\n      in imagination-based actor-critic?\\\\n      (3) Contribution: closed causal chain (trained dt_emb → nve>1.5x → stochastic collapse) + practical mitigation\\\\n      (dt=1 imagination, 95% recovery). Diagnostic methodology with factorial design.\\\\n      (4) Scope: DreamerV3/RSSM, Walker Walk (+ cross-env if ready).\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C6]\\\\n    key_references: [hafner2023dreamerv3, nhu2025tawm, lu2018nondelusional, gumbsch2024thick]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 6\\\\n\\\\n  - id: related_work\\\\n    title: Related Work\\\\n    target_pages: 1.0\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) Temporal abstraction in RL: options (Sutton 1999), FiGAR, TempoRL, SDAR — all model-free.\\\\n      (2) World-model RL & imagination: DreamerV1-V4, IRIS, TWM — standard dt=1 imagination.\\\\n      (3) Variable-rate world models: TAWM (MPC, beneficial), THICK/Hieros (hierarchy), MTS3, LS-Imagine.\\\\n      (4) Value overestimation in MBRL: MBPO, MOPO, delusional bias (Lu 2018), MAD-TD.\\\\n      (5) Diagnostic methodology precedent: Implementation Matters, What Matters for Actor-Critic.\\\\n      Differentiate from TAWM (MPC vs imagination paradigm — opposite conclusions on Δt conditioning).\\\\n    claims_referenced: []\\\\n    key_references: [sutton1999options, sharma2017figar, biedenkapp2021temporl, hafner2023dreamerv3,\\\\n                     nhu2025tawm, gumbsch2024thick, mattes2024hieros, shaj2023mts3, li2025lsimagine,\\\\n                     janner2019mbpo, yu2020mopo, lu2018nondelusional, su2020conqur,\\\\n                     engstrom2020implementation, andrychowicz2021whatmatters, frauenknecht2025rollouts]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 7\\\\n\\\\n  - id: methodology\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Experimental Setup\\\\\\\"\\\\n    target_pages: 1.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) DreamerV3 base architecture (RSSM, symlog, discrete latents) — brief, cite original.\\\\n      (2) Variable-rate imagination mechanism: dt_embedding (trained/untrained/removed), temporal subsampling,\\\\n      imagination horizon H. How each factor modifies imagination rollouts.\\\\n      (3) Factorial design: 2×2×2 grid (dt_emb training × subsample × H) + fixed-dt baselines + mitigation.\\\\n      Present grid as table with cell assignments.\\\\n      (4) Diagnostic metrics: eval return, v/e ratio, normalized v/e (nve = exp_v/e / baseline_v/e at same step),\\\\n      nve>1.5x threshold, RSSM fidelity (obs_MSE, reward_MAE at dt=1 vs dt=2).\\\\n      (5) Environment: Walker Walk (DMC), 500K baseline / 105K treatments, 2+ seeds per config.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6]\\\\n    key_references: [hafner2023dreamerv3, agarwal2021precipice]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 2\\\\n\\\\n  - id: results\\\\n    title: Results\\\\n    target_pages: 2.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      Organized by findings (F1-F6 mapping to C1-C6):\\\\n      F1 (C1): All dt>1 degrade — learning curves overlay (exp_001, 005, 006, 007).\\\\n      F2 (C2): Trained dt_emb → nve>1.5x (4/4 separation). 008d vs 008f causal control.\\\\n      Stochastic collapse: 008d seed 1 sustained nve>1.5x → collapse; 009b seed 2 transient → self-correction.\\\\n      F3 (C3): Untrained dt_emb prevents drift — 008a@105K=778, nve 0.59-0.93x.\\\\n      F4 (C4): dt=2 > dt=4 monotonic degradation.\\\\n      F5 (C5): Horizon/subsample secondary — 008c (H=8) vs 008a (H=15).\\\\n      F6 (C6): dt=1 imagination mitigation — 008e_v3@105K=869.9 (95% baseline).\\\\n      [D035] C6 currently has 1 independent seed (seed=1). s0 and s1 are both --seed 1 (deterministic reproduction,\\\\n      NOT cross-seed consistency). 008e_v3_s2 (seed=2, RUNNING) is the first independent seed verification.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C1, C2, C3, C4, C5, C6]\\\\n    experiments_required:\\\\n      - exp_001_baseline  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_005_event_gated_v4  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_006_fixed_dt2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_007_fixed_dt4  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008c_no_subsample_dt2_h8  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008d_subsample_on_h8  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15  # DONE (seed=1)\\\\n      - exp_008f_no_dt_embed_subsample_on_h8  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_009b_008d_walker_s2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_009c_008f_walker_s2  # DONE\\\\n      - exp_008e_v3_walker_s1  # DONE (seed=1, deterministic reproduction of s0)\\\\n      - exp_008e_v3_walker_s2  # RUNNING (seed=2, first independent C6 seed)\\\\n      - exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2  # RUNNING\\\\n    data_ready: partial  # 008e_v3_s2 and baseline_s2 still running\\\\n    writing_order: 1  # write first — data-rich, anchors everything\\\\n\\\\n  - id: analysis\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Analysis & Discussion\\\\\\\"\\\\n    target_pages: 1.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      (1) Mechanism: trained dt_emb enables reward head to produce systematically biased dt>1 predictions\\\\n      (reward gap 2.78x in 008d). Critic trained on these → optimistic value landscape → actor exploitation.\\\\n      RSSM fidelity table: absolute errors + ratios side-by-side.\\\\n      (2) Stochastic collapse: why sustained vs transient nve>1.5x diverges (plasticity, primacy bias).\\\\n      Connect to Zhang 2026, Lyle 2022, Bjorck 2022.\\\\n      (3) Why MPC is immune: TAWM uses Δt conditioning successfully because MPC re-plans from real states.\\\\n      Imagination-based training accumulates value error across full rollout → exploit.\\\\n      (4) 008f trade-off: removing dt_emb eliminates delusional critic but destroys reward prediction (75x MAE).\\\\n      008e_v3 as the correct fix (keeps trained dt_emb, restricts imagination to dt=1).\\\\n      (5) Implications: current RSSM insufficient for dt>1 imagination; hierarchy (THICK, Hieros) as correct direction.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C2, C3, C6]\\\\n    key_references: [nhu2025tawm, lu2018nondelusional, zhang2026instability, lyle2022capacity,\\\\n                     lee2024dreamsmooth, ma2024harmonydream, gumbsch2024thick, mattes2024hieros]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 3\\\\n\\\\n  - id: conclusion\\\\n    title: Conclusion\\\\n    target_pages: 0.5\\\\n    content_outline: |\\\\n      Summarize causal chain. Practical takeaway: use dt=1 imagination even with multi-dt training data.\\\\n      Limitations: single environment (Walker Walk) primary, DreamerV3/RSSM-specific.\\\\n      Future: uncertainty-gated imagination truncation, hierarchical approaches, improved RSSM fidelity.\\\\n    claims_referenced: [C2, C6]\\\\n    data_ready: true\\\\n    writing_order: 9\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# FIGURES\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nfigures:\\\\n  - id: fig1_learning_curves\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Learning curves across all configurations\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Hero figure. All experiments overlaid showing systematic degradation pattern.\\\\n      Groups: baseline (dt=1), fixed dt>1 (006, 007), learned gate (005),\\\\n      factorial ablations (008a-f), mitigation (008e_v3).\\\\n    data_source: [exp_001_baseline, exp_005_event_gated_v4, exp_006_fixed_dt2, exp_007_fixed_dt4,\\\\n                  exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2, exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15]\\\\n    placement: results (F1/C1)\\\\n    status: data_ready  # all experiments DONE\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig2_nve_trajectory\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Normalized value/eval ratio trajectories — diagnostic marker\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      nve over training steps for key experiments. 1.5x threshold line marked.\\\\n      Show: 008d seed 1 (sustained >1.5x → collapse), 009b seed 2 (transient >1.5x → self-correction),\\\\n      008f seeds (both <1.5x), 008e_v3 (healthy, ~0.80x). 4/4 separation at threshold.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_009b_008d_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008f_no_dt_embed_subsample_on_h8, exp_009c_008f_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15, exp_001_baseline]\\\\n    placement: results (F2/C2)\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig3_factorial_grid\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Factorial experiment summary (2×2 grid)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      2×2 grid: dt_emb (trained/untrained) × subsample (ON/OFF), with H as secondary axis.\\\\n      Each cell shows final eval return + nve status (healthy/pathological).\\\\n      Clearly shows trained dt_emb as the separating factor.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2, exp_008c_no_subsample_dt2_h8,\\\\n                  exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_006_fixed_dt2]\\\\n    placement: results (F2-F5)\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig4_mechanism_diagram\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Causal mechanism diagram\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Flow diagram: trained dt_embedding → RSSM dt>1 predictions (low fidelity) →\\\\n      reward head systematic bias (2.78x gap) → critic value overestimation (nve>1.5x) →\\\\n      actor exploits overestimated values → performance collapse (stochastic gate: sustained vs transient).\\\\n      Include dt=1 imagination as \\\\\\\"circuit breaker\\\\\\\" at the imagination step.\\\\n    data_source: []  # conceptual figure\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    status: ready_to_draw\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig5_dt_amplification\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Performance vs dt (monotonic degradation)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Bar or line chart: dt=1 (baseline ~950) > dt=2 (peak 485) > dt=4 (peak 177).\\\\n      Clear monotonic relationship.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_001_baseline, exp_006_fixed_dt2, exp_007_fixed_dt4]\\\\n    placement: results (F4/C4)\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fig6_mitigation\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Mitigation comparison: dt=1 imagination recovers 95% baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Side-by-side or overlay: baseline, 008e_v3 (mitigation, 95%), 008a (untrained dt_emb, 85%),\\\\n      006 (trained dt_emb + dt>1, collapse). Shows mitigation is best non-baseline option.\\\\n      [D035] 008e_v3 s0 and s1 are both seed=1 (deterministic reproduction) — plot as single seed=1 line.\\\\n      Add s2 (seed=2, RUNNING) when complete for true multi-seed evidence. Do NOT present s0+s1 as two independent seeds.\\\\n      Can add a reproducibility footnote: \\\\\\\"deterministic reproduction confirmed (869.88 vs 869.9)\\\\\\\".\\\\n    data_source: [exp_001_baseline, exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15,\\\\n                  exp_008a_no_subsample_dt2, exp_006_fixed_dt2,\\\\n                  exp_008e_v3_walker_s2]  # s2 when DONE\\\\n    placement: results (F6/C6)\\\\n    status: partial  # s2 RUNNING — first independent seed\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# TABLES\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\ntables:\\\\n  - id: tab1_rssm_fidelity\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"RSSM prediction fidelity at dt=1 vs dt=2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Three models (baseline, 008d collapsed, 008f no-dt-emb) × two metrics (obs_MSE, reward_MAE)\\\\n      × two dt values (1, 2). Report absolute values AND ratios. Key: 008d reward gap 2.78x\\\\n      (delusional source), 008f reward gap 1.01x (no distinction → no exploitation but also no learning).\\\\n    data_source: [exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis]\\\\n    placement: analysis\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: tab2_factorial_summary\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Factorial experiment design and results\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Full grid showing all experimental conditions and key outcomes.\\\\n      Columns: exp_id, dt_emb (trained/untrained/none), subsample, H, dt_imag, final_eval,\\\\n      nve_peak, collapse_status.\\\\n    data_source: [all_experiments]\\\\n    placement: methodology/results\\\\n    status: data_ready\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n  - id: tab3_multi_seed\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Multi-seed results summary\\\\\\\"\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      Per-config seed results with IQM. Show 008d (1/2 collapse), 008f (0/2 collapse),\\\\n      baseline (0/2 collapse).\\\\n      [D035] 008e_v3: currently 1 independent seed (seed=1, deterministically reproduced twice).\\\\n      s2 (seed=2, RUNNING) is the first independent seed — update table when done.\\\\n      Do NOT count s0+s1 as two independent seeds.\\\\n    data_source: [exp_008d_subsample_on_h8, exp_009b_008d_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008f_no_dt_embed_subsample_on_h8, exp_009c_008f_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_008e_v3_subsample_on_dt1_h15, exp_008e_v3_walker_s2,\\\\n                  exp_001_baseline, exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2]\\\\n    placement: results\\\\n    status: partial  # baseline_s2 and 008e_v3_s2 still RUNNING\\\\n    gpu_cost: 0\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# WRITING ORDER (by dependency)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - order: 1\\\\n    section: results\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Data-rich, anchors all other sections. Most figures/tables go here.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: null\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 2\\\\n    section: methodology\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Defines experiment design referenced by results. Can write in parallel with results.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: null\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 3\\\\n    section: analysis\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Interprets results, requires results section to be stable.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: results\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 4\\\\n    section: related_work\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"literature_map complete (72 papers). Position against TAWM, THICK, Hieros.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: null  # can write early\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 5\\\\n    section: introduction\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Frames contributions — needs results and analysis solidified.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: [results, analysis]\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 6\\\\n    section: conclusion\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Summarizes; last content section.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: [results, analysis]\\\\n\\\\n  - order: 7\\\\n    section: abstract\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Written last, distills entire paper.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    blocker: [introduction, results, analysis, conclusion]\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# LITERATURE STRATEGY\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nliterature:\\\\n  must_cite:\\\\n    - hafner2023dreamerv3  # base system\\\\n    - hafner2020dreamerv1  # architecture family\\\\n    - hafner2021dreamerv2  # discrete latents predecessor\\\\n    - sutton1999options  # temporal abstraction foundation\\\\n    - lu2018nondelusional  # delusional bias theory\\\\n    - nhu2025tawm  # closest competitor — MUST differentiate MPC vs imagination\\\\n    - gumbsch2024thick  # hierarchical alternative in Dreamer\\\\n    - mattes2024hieros  # hierarchical imagination\\\\n    - janner2019mbpo  # model exploitation in MBRL\\\\n    - agarwal2021precipice  # evaluation methodology (IQM)\\\\n    - henderson2018deep  # seed variance\\\\n    - frauenknecht2025rollouts  # imagination rollout quality (ICLR 2025)\\\\n    - lee2024dreamsmooth  # reward prediction bottleneck\\\\n    - zhang2026instability  # training instability dynamics\\\\n\\\\n  should_cite:\\\\n    - li2025lsimagine  # concurrent Dreamer horizon extension\\\\n    - shaj2023mts3  # multi-rate dynamics foundation\\\\n    - sharma2017figar  # FiGAR — learned action repeat\\\\n    - biedenkapp2021temporl  # TempoRL — model-free temporal abstraction\\\\n    - fujimoto2018td3  # overestimation in actor-critic\\\\n    - vanhasselt2016double  # double Q-learning\\\\n    - yu2020mopo  # pessimistic MBRL\\\\n    - su2020conqur  # delusional bias mitigation\\\\n    - tallec2019making  # time discretization sensitivity\\\\n    - engstrom2020implementation  # diagnostic methodology precedent\\\\n    - andrychowicz2021whatmatters  # factorial study precedent\\\\n    - lyle2022capacity  # necessary vs sufficient conditions\\\\n    - bjorck2022variance  # early outlier runs\\\\n    - qiao2023mind  # primacy bias in MBRL\\\\n    - ma2024harmonydream  # obs vs reward prediction balance\\\\n    - voelcker2025madtd  # value misgeneralization\\\\n    - hafner2025dreamerv4  # DreamerV4 (scope limitation discussion)\\\\n\\\\n  consider_citing:\\\\n    - zhang2026hwm  # hierarchical world model planning\\\\n    - park2021sar  # time-discretization invariant action repeat\\\\n    - nikishin2022primacy  # primacy bias\\\\n    - sokar2023dormant  # dormant neurons\\\\n    - lyle2024normalization  # normalization & effective LR\\\\n    - kumar2022dr3  # feature aliasing\\\\n    - hansen2024tdmpc2  # TD-MPC2 (contrast MPC paradigm)\\\\n    - hafner2022director  # hierarchical Dreamer\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# RISK ASSESSMENT\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\nrisks:\\\\n  - id: risk_cross_env\\\\n    severity: medium\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Cheetah Run / Cartpole experiments still QUEUED (exp_010a). No cross-environment data.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Scope claims to Walker Walk + DreamerV3. Discuss generalizability as future work. If 010a finishes by May 27, include.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C1]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: [exp_010a_cheetah_baseline_s1]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_c6_seed2\\\\n    severity: high  # D035: upgraded from low — s2 is first independent seed, not bonus\\\\n    description: |\\\\n      [D035] 008e_v3 s0 and s1 are BOTH seed=1 (deterministic reproduction, NOT independent seeds).\\\\n      C6 currently has only 1 independent seed data point. 008e_v3_s2 (seed=2, RUNNING) is the\\\\n      FIRST independent seed verification — it is critical, not a bonus.\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"s2 RUNNING, ETA ~6h. If s2 confirms (~870), can claim 2-seed consistency. If s2 diverges, C6 strength weakens significantly.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C6]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: [exp_008e_v3_walker_s2]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_baseline_s2\\\\n    severity: low\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2 RUNNING. Needed for multi-seed baseline reference.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Already have s0 (exp_001, 915.67). Can report 2-seed results if s2 not done.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C1, C2, C3]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: [exp_009a_baseline_walker_s2]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_collapse_probability\\\\n    severity: low\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"exp_009e (008d seed 1 repeat) QUEUED — would narrow collapse probability from 1/2 to 1/3 or 2/3.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Current 1/2 is honest and transparent. Report as 'stochastic (1/2 seeds)' with caveat.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependent_claims: [C2]\\\\n    blocking_experiments: [exp_009e_008d_walker_s1]\\\\n\\\\n  - id: risk_page_budget\\\\n    severity: medium\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"8 pages tight for 6 claims + factorial design + RSSM analysis + multi-seed.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    mitigation: \\\\\\\"Prioritize C1, C2, C6 in main text. C3-C5 can be condensed. Use appendix for extended data.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# TIMELINE\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n\\\\ntimeline:\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-15\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Writing plan finalized. Begin Results + Methodology drafting.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-17\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Results draft complete. All figures generated (0 GPU cost).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-19\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Analysis & Discussion draft. Related Work draft.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-21\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Introduction draft. Full paper skeleton assembled.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-23\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Internal review pass. Abstract + Conclusion. Page budget check.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-25\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Revision pass. Incorporate any new experiment results (RUNNING → DONE).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-27\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Final polish. Reference check. Supplementary materials.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - date: 2026-05-29\\\\n    milestone: \\\\\\\"Submission deadline.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 20067, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01572bQizBubcV4Kjo3jZRQ1","session_id":"aa49a6eb-652d-4e6b-ad9c-09d11a6223fd","uuid":"c1d16338-9d36-4074-88ff-a691524cf2f4","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:03:00.779Z"}
