{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013EqmuFjYSCeELwN4PSEkf4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n2\t\n3\t## Title Candidates\n4\t\n5\t1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in DreamerV3: A Diagnostic Analysis of Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n6\t2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in DreamerV3's Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n7\t3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation from Temporal Abstraction in DreamerV3\"**\n8\t\n9\t## Venue\n10\t\n11\t**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n12\t\n13\t## Narrative Positioning\n14\t\n15\tThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n16\t\n17\tThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor, plus a **practical mitigation guideline** (restrict imagination to dt=1 during multi-dt training → 95% baseline recovery). Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n18\t\n19\tWe scope all claims to **DreamerV3 and its RSSM world model**. Generalizability to other latent-dynamics architectures is discussed but not claimed.\n20\t\n21\t---\n22\t\n23\t## Core Claims\n24\t\n25\t### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n26\t\n27\tTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n28\t\n29\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n30\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n31\t| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n32\t| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n33\t| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n34\t| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n35\t\n36\t**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n37\t\n38\t### C2: Trained dt_embedding reliably triggers pathological value overestimation (>1.5x), creating high collapse risk\n39\t\n40\t**D032 update: nve>1.5x threshold has perfect separating power (4/4); collapse itself is stochastic.**\n41\t\n42\tThe trained dt_embedding reliably induces pathological value overestimation (normalized v/e >1.5x baseline) across all tested seeds, but whether this overestimation progresses to catastrophic performance collapse is stochastic:\n43\t\n44\t- **WITH trained dt_emb**: 2/2 seeds exceed nve>1.5x at 35K+ (008d seed 1: sustained 1.71x@35K→2.09x@45K→4.12x@55K → collapse; 009b seed 2: 1.62x@45K → self-correction to 0.38x@105K)\n45\t- **WITHOUT dt_emb (008f)**: 0/2 seeds exceed nve>1.5x at 35K+ (seed 1 peak 1.02x@25K; seed 2 peak 1.26x@25K)\n46\t- **1.5x threshold (35K+)**: 4/4 perfect classification — reliable diagnostic marker separating trained vs untrained dt_emb\n47\t\n48\t**⚠️ 时间限定**: nve>1.5x 诊断适用于 **35K+ steps**（此时 baseline v/e 已充分收敛至 >0.24，比率稳定可靠）。25K 处 baseline v/e 仅 0.087，微小绝对差异可被放大为大比率（如 009b@25K nve=2.05x 和 008e_v3@25K nve=1.93x 均为 false positive）。论文中报告 threshold 时必须标注此限定。\n49\t\n50\t**Sustained vs transient overestimation**: The key difference between collapse (008d seed 1) and self-correction (009b seed 2) is the **temporal persistence** of nve>1.5x. Seed 1 maintained nve>1.5x across 3 consecutive checkpoints at 35K+ (1.71x@35K→2.09x@45K→4.12x@55K, accelerating), locking the positive feedback loop; seed 2 exceeded 1.5x at 45K (1.62x) but dropped to 1.41x@55K and continued declining, allowing self-correction. This suggests a \"point of no return\" where sustained overestimation becomes irreversible, with early training stochasticity (initialization, data sampling order) determining which path is taken (cf. Henderson et al. 2018, Bjorck et al. 2022, Qiao et al. 2023).\n51\t\n52\tThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies. Without dt_embedding conditioning, the overestimation feedback loop is blocked entirely (nve never exceeds 1.5x).\n53\t\n54\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n55\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n56\t| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n57\t| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n58\t| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n59\t| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n60\t| **D032: Trained dt_emb seed 2 — pathological but self-correcting** | exp_009b (008d config, seed 2) | eval 39→141→164→141→172→209→197→236→279→268@105K (**no collapse**, rising). nve: **2.05x@25K**→1.24x→**1.62x@45K**→1.41x→0.94x→0.66x→0.51x→0.43x→**0.38x@105K**. Transient nve>1.5x with self-correction. Value peaked 110.9@65K → self-corrected to 67.3@105K while eval improved. |\n61\t| **1.5x threshold separating power** | 008d+009b vs 008f+009c | WITH trained dt_emb: 2/2 seeds exceed nve>1.5x (008d peak 2.09x sustained, 009b peak 2.05x transient). WITHOUT dt_emb: 0/2 seeds exceed nve>1.5x (008f peak 1.02x, 009c peak 1.26x). **4/4 perfect classification.** |\n62\t| **Causal control: dt_embed_dim=0 (direction confirmed, seed-dependent)** | exp_008f seed 1 + exp_009c seed 2 | **Seed 1**: eval 197→207→194→173→503@105K (zigzag recovery); nve 1.02x→0.73x→0.83x→0.97x→0.30x. **Seed 2**: eval 169→211→239→359→227→191→148@105K (decline after 75K); nve 1.26x→0.79x→0.72x→0.33x→0.60x→0.90x→1.14x. Both vs 008d@45K nve=2.09x: onset delayed 60K+ steps, severity reduced ~2x. **009c extending to 200K to observe if nve crosses 1.5x.** |\n63\t| RSSM fidelity analysis | baseline / 008d / 008f | See RSSM Fidelity Table below |\n64\t\n65\t**⚠️ 008f 定位：因果控制实验，非推荐方案。** 008f 去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward_MAE=0.747（baseline 的 75x），reward head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2（reward gap 仅 1.01x vs 008d 的 2.78x）。**D030 更新**：008f seed 2 (009c) 在 105K 达到 nve=1.14x（borderline），seed 1 为 0.30x——protection 不 robust。但 008f 两个 seed 的 v/e 增长速度均显著慢于 008d（008d@45K=2.09x vs 008f seed 2@105K=1.14x），确认 dt_embedding 是 primary amplifier。**C2 因果方向成立，但 \"eliminates\" 改为 \"significantly delays and reduces\"。推荐方案仍是 008e_v3（C6）**。\n66\t\n67\t**RSSM Fidelity Table（论文中必须同时报告绝对误差和比率）：**\n68\t\n69\t| Model | dt1 obs_MSE | dt2 obs_MSE | obs gap | dt1 reward_MAE | dt2 reward_MAE | reward gap |\n70\t|-------|------------|------------|---------|---------------|---------------|------------|\n71\t| baseline (exp_001) | 13.49 | 27.50 | **2.04x** | 0.0102 | 0.0159 | 1.56x |\n72\t| 008d (trained dt_emb, collapsed) | 41.31 | 53.67 | **1.30x** | 0.0568 | 0.1579 | **2.78x** |\n73\t| 008f (no dt_emb, stable) | 8.01 | 22.04 | **2.75x** | 0.7469 | 0.7526 | 1.01x |\n74\t\n75\t**解读要点**：008d 的低 obs gap ratio (1.30x) 具有误导性——其 dt=1 绝对误差本身已是 baseline 的 3x（模型已崩塌）。论文中必须并排呈现绝对误差和比率，避免审稿人被比率误导。\n76\t\n77\t**Strength**: Moderate-strong (D032 update: causal direction + diagnostic marker confirmed; collapse stochastic). The **nve>1.5x threshold** achieves 4/4 perfect separation: all trained dt_emb seeds (008d, 009b) exceed 1.5x; no untrained seeds (008f, 009c) exceed 1.5x. This is the paper's strongest quantitative result for C2. **Collapse** is stochastic (1/2 trained seeds): 008d seed 1 shows sustained nve>1.5x → collapse; 009b seed 2 shows transient nve>1.5x → self-correction. The **causal direction** is unambiguous across all 4 data points. Pending: 009e (008d seed 1) to determine collapse probability (1/3 vs 2/3); 009f (008f seed 1) for third untrained seed; 009c extension to 200K.\n78\t\n79\t### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n80\t\n81\tWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete zigzag recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n82\t\n83\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n84\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n85\t| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n86\t| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n87\t| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n88\t| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n89\t| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n90\t\n91\t**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete zigzag recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n92\t\n93\t**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n94\t\n95\t**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n96\t\n97\t### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n98\t\n99\tIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n100\t\n101\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n102\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n103\t| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n104\t| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n105\t| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n106\t\n107\t**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n108\t\n109\t### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n110\t\n111\tSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n112\t\n113\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n114\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n115\t| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n116\t| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n117\t| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n118\t| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n119\t| Subsample ON, trained dt_emb, dt=1 imag, no collapse | exp_008e_v3 (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, dt=1 imag, H=15) | eval 382@45K (86% baseline); normalized v/e 0.88x@45K (normal). Even with trained dt_emb and subsample ON, restricting imagination to dt=1 prevents collapse |\n120\t\n121\t**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. exp_008e_v3 confirms subsample ON does not trigger collapse when imagination is restricted to dt=1, even with trained dt_emb. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n122\t\n123\t### C6: Restricting imagination to dt=1 during multi-dt training provides practical mitigation\n124\t\n125\tWhen training with multi-dt data (subsample ON, dt∈{1,2}) while restricting imagination rollouts to dt=1, performance recovers to 95% of the dt=1 baseline. This provides a concrete, zero-cost mitigation guideline: keep imagination at dt=1 even if the world model learns multi-dt dynamics.\n126\t\n127\t**008f reward 退化发现进一步强化 C6 的价值**：008f（去掉 dt_embedding）虽避免崩塌但 reward 预测退化 75x；而 008e_v3（保留 trained dt_emb + dt=1 imagination）达到 95% baseline 且 reward prediction 不受影响。008e_v3 是唯一同时避免崩塌且保持完整预测能力的配置。**关键洞察：008d（trained dt_emb + dt>1 imag）collapse vs 008e_v3（trained dt_emb + dt=1 imag）healthy，证明 critical variable 是 imagination dt，不是 embedding 训练状态。不需要改动模型架构，只需改 imagination 策略。**\n128\t\n129\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n130\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n131\t| dt=1 imagination + multi-dt training | exp_008e_v3 (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, dt=1 imag, H=15) | eval_return_105K=869.9 (95% of baseline 915.67), normalized v/e=0.80x |\n132\t| Comparison: dt=2 imagination collapses | exp_006 (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, dt=2 imag, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse. v/e 2.3x baseline@55K |\n133\t| Comparison: untrained dt_emb + dt=2 degrades | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, dt=2 imag, H=15) | 778@105K (85% baseline). Better than collapse but 10pp below mitigation |\n134\t| Comparison: no dt_emb avoids collapse but degrades reward | exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0, subsample ON, H=8) | No collapse, but reward_MAE=0.747 (75x baseline). Avoidance of collapse comes at cost of reward prediction |\n135\t\n136\t**Strength**: Moderate-strong → **strengthened by 008f contrast**. 008e_v3 is the only configuration that (a) avoids delusional critic collapse, (b) maintains healthy reward prediction, AND (c) achieves near-baseline performance (95%). Single seed, single environment; multi-seed + cross-environment planned (P0). Actionable: practitioners using variable-dt training data should restrict imagination to dt=1 until RSSM fidelity at dt>1 improves.\n137\t\n138\t---\n139\t\n140\t## Story Arc\n141\t\n142\t### 1. Introduction\n143\t- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n144\t- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n145\t- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n146\t- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding as the reliable trigger for pathological value overestimation (nve>1.5x, 4/4 separating power), with collapse as a stochastic consequence, plus a practical mitigation guideline (dt=1 imagination → 95% baseline)\n147\t\n148\t### 2. Background & Related Work\n149\t- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n150\t- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n151\t- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n152\t- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n153\t\n154\t### 3. Methodology\n155\t- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n156\t- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n157\t- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n158\t- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n159\t\n160\t### 4. Results\n161\t- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n162\t- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n163\t- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n164\t- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n165\t- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n166\t- **Finding 6**: Restricting imagination to dt=1 during multi-dt training recovers 95% baseline — practical mitigation (C6)\n167\t\n168\t### 5. Discussion\n169\t- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n170\t- RSSM fidelity analysis: 008d reward gap (2.78x) vs 008f reward gap (1.01x) — trained dt_emb 让 reward head 在 dt=2 时产生系统性偏差，这是 critic 被误导的直接来源\n171\t- 008f 的 reward 退化 trade-off：去掉 dt_embedding 避免崩塌但牺牲 reward 预测质量；008e_v3 是更优方案\n172\t- Connection to existing theory: non-delusional Q-learning (Lu et al., 2018), model exploitation in MBRL\n173\t- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n174\t- **D032: Value self-correction mechanism (009b)**: 009b (008d seed 2) demonstrates that pathological overestimation (nve>1.5x) is not always irreversible. Value peaked at 110.9@65K then monotonically self-corrected to 67.3@105K, while eval simultaneously improved (172→268). Hypothesized mechanism: when the critic's overestimation does not yet dominate the actor's gradient signal (transient vs sustained nve>1.5x), the actor can still learn from real environment returns, creating a corrective force. In 008d seed 1, the sustained overestimation (3 consecutive checkpoints >1.5x at 35K+) overwhelmed this correction. The bifurcation likely depends on early training stochasticity — initialization and data sampling order determine whether the overestimation feedback loop locks in before correction can take hold (consistent with primacy bias in MBRL, Qiao et al. 2023; early outlier runs, Bjorck et al. 2022). This makes nve>1.5x a **necessary condition** for collapse but not sufficient — the temporal persistence of overestimation is the second gate.\n175\t\n176\t### 6. Implications for Future Work\n177\t- Don't use dt>1 imagination with trained dt_embedding in current world-model architectures (trained dt_emb is safe if imagination stays at dt=1)\n178\t- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n179\t- Imagination-side restriction (dt=1 imagination with multi-dt training) as the practical mitigation — no architecture change needed\n180\t- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n181\t\n182\t---\n183\t\n184\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n185\t\n186\t### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n187\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n188\t**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n189\t\n190\t### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n191\t**Pre-emption**: Beyond diagnosis, we provide a **concrete mitigation guideline**: train with multi-dt data but restrict imagination rollouts to dt=1. exp_008e_v3 demonstrates this recovers 95% of baseline performance (869.9 vs 915.67) with normalized v/e=0.80x (healthy). This is zero-cost to implement and directly actionable.\n192\t**Mitigation**: Present 008e_v3 as a practical recommendation in Section 6. Additionally, we outline an uncertainty-gated imagination truncation direction as future work.\n193\t\n194\t### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n195\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n196\t**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n197\t\n198\t### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n199\t**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n200\t**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ULYQdJC4FEnAQtNq7j8RxB","session_id":"aa49a6eb-652d-4e6b-ad9c-09d11a6223fd","uuid":"220e50cd-15e2-4e97-ac5f-177f345f29c5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:03:47.095Z"}
